  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-or600.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Or 603.02 Exemptions to Groundwater Quality Criteria",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Or 603.02 Exemptions to Groundwater Quality Criteria. Groundwater quality shall be exempt from the groundwater quality criteria of Env-Or 603.01 if:\n\n(a) The groundwater is within a groundwater discharge zone permitted in accordance with Env-Wq 402;\n\n(b) The groundwater is within a groundwater management zone permitted in accordance with Env-Or 607;\n\n(c) The groundwater is contaminated solely with salt and other de-icing chemicals applied for winter road maintenance;\n\n(d) The groundwater contamination resulted from backwash from a public water treatment facility that is subject to Env-Wq 402; or\n\n(e) The groundwater contamination is not the result of human operations or activities.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Or 600) #8812, eff 2-1-07; ss by #10831, eff 6-1-15; ss by #14419, eff 11-4-25, EXPIRES: 11-4-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-or600.html"
